      "evidence": {
        "EV-LV-A1-T1": {
          "artifact_ref": "keyring/spec/credential-revocation.md",
          "content": "## Credentials — revocation\n\nA client credential can be revoked by its owner or by an operator. Revocation takes\neffect immediately and cannot be undone by the client.\n\nNormative rule\n1. After a credential has been revoked, no authentication attempt that presents it may\n   succeed.\n\nExample\nCredential K-17 is revoked at 09:00:00. A login presenting K-17 at 09:00:30 is refused.\n",
          "content_sha256": "62b843a41e668abe3fb4a62432e115d149eb3a55b4f614f667000883cff514e3",
          "evidence_id": "EV-LV-A1-T1",
          "observed_at": "2026-09-15T00:00:00Z",
          "project_id": "PROJ-LV-ALPHA",
          "scope": [
            "keyring"
          ],
          "source_kind": "DOCUMENT",
          "source_ref": "experiment://locus-validation/alpha/T1/A1",
          "supersedes_evidence_id": null
        },
        "EV-LV-A2-T1": {
          "artifact_ref": "keyring/spec/retry-timing.md",
          "content": "## Job execution — retry timing\n\nWhen an execution of a job fails, the scheduler retries the job later rather than at\nonce, so that a struggling dependency is not hammered.\n\nNormative rule\n1. The delay before each retry is double the delay before the previous retry, starting\n   from two seconds for the first retry.\n\nExample\nJob J-4 fails three times; the scheduler waits 2 s, then 4 s, then 8 s before each\nretry.\n",
          "content_sha256": "2d97d5568554b30d07e752469c10f8a84a298a281c4474e59fe404670b59ca88",
          "evidence_id": "EV-LV-A2-T1",
          "observed_at": "2026-09-15T00:00:00Z",
          "project_id": "PROJ-LV-ALPHA",
          "scope": [
            "keyring"
          ],
          "source_kind": "DOCUMENT",
          "source_ref": "experiment://locus-validation/alpha/T1/A2",
          "supersedes_evidence_id": null
        },
        "EV-LV-A3-T1": {
          "artifact_ref": "keyring/spec/worker-lease.md",
          "content": "## Worker lease — duration\n\nA worker holds a lease on the job it is executing so that no other worker picks the\nsame job up.\n\nNormative rule\n1. A lease lasts 90 seconds from the moment it is granted.\n\nExample\nA lease granted at 10:00:00 expires at 10:01:30.\n",
          "content_sha256": "5caf28ce993bf53b9ed074dd9ccefc1354633c0d0733fc923c90986da7a24b2d",
          "evidence_id": "EV-LV-A3-T1",
          "observed_at": "2026-09-15T00:00:00Z",
          "project_id": "PROJ-LV-ALPHA",
          "scope": [
            "keyring"
          ],
          "source_kind": "DOCUMENT",
          "source_ref": "experiment://locus-validation/alpha/T1/A3",
          "supersedes_evidence_id": null
        },
        "EV-LV-A4-T1": {
          "artifact_ref": "keyring/spec/execution-time-limit.md",
          "content": "## Execution — time limit\n\nA stalled execution must not hold its worker indefinitely.\n\nNormative rule\n1. A single execution may run for at most 30 seconds; when the limit is reached the\n   execution is stopped and recorded as a failure.\n\nExample\nAn execution that starts at 11:00:00 and is still running at 11:00:30 is stopped and\nrecorded as failed.\n",
          "content_sha256": "6bf7b166b468327941b40475b3739f51e87dd33e950464089a867a101a92b982",
          "evidence_id": "EV-LV-A4-T1",
          "observed_at": "2026-09-15T00:00:00Z",
          "project_id": "PROJ-LV-ALPHA",
          "scope": [
            "keyring"
          ],
          "source_kind": "DOCUMENT",
          "source_ref": "experiment://locus-validation/alpha/T1/A4",
          "supersedes_evidence_id": null
        }
      },
